       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day, and that holds for an adult with normal kidney and liver function. A dose that high carries a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity.\n\nDid you mean a different dose? These are the usual adult ranges:\n- **Depression, OCD, and similar conditions:** start at 50 mg once daily, with a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg per day.\n- **Panic disorder, PTSD, and social anxiety disorder:** start at 25 mg once daily, then increase to 50 mg after one week.\n\nIf you give me the intended dose, I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter 100 mg by mouth once daily. If you really do need more than 200 mg per day, please take that up with pharmacy or the prescribing physician. I can't enter a dose over the labeled maximum."
      }
